# This is NOT the AuraFS product handbook.
# AuraFS keeps its own rules inside aurafs/ when that product is in play.
# This file is law for the ecosystem: TSLCA, FTQC, TVFD, VIM, SUXS, SAGES, APS-OKF.
#
# Authority chain (read in this order when a conflict appears):
#   1. .cursorrules                 this file — how you may edit
#   2. aps.toml                     machine registry and shared numbers
#   3. INVARIANTS.md                organism locks
#   4. PHYSICS.md                   shared constants
#   5. <folder>/INVARIANTS.md       volume locks
#   6. <folder>/PHYSICS.md          volume numbers
#   7. <folder>/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md  Cursor briefing for that folder
#   8. APS_OKF_SCHEMA.md            Aurphyx-internal header law
#   9. aps-okf.yaml / aps-okf.md    public header contract
#  10. GATEKEEPERS.md               what may change
#  11. APS_NAMING_EPOCHS.md         retired names
#  12. SCIENTIFIC_CODEX.md          how math is written
#  13. AURPHYX_CODEX.md             what each folder is
#  14. MYTHIC_CODEX.md              story only — never metadata
#
# If a listed file does not exist yet, do not invent its contents as you go.
# Flag the gap. Keep editing under this file and existing sources.
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §1 — STANCE
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

These frameworks are CANON. Treat them as factual working systems.

- TSLCA, FTQC, TVFD, VIM, Theory of Balance, Balance Continuum, SAGES, SUXS, APS-OKF are locked architecture.
- IBM Qiskit results and completed simulations are evidence. Do not demand wet-lab validation before treating equations as the working definition.
- Do not hedge as “myth,” “allegory,” “unverified speculation,” or “spiritual framework.”
- Narrative mappings (Hecate, Maiden/Mother/Crone, 3-6-9-13 story) live only in MYTHIC_CODEX.md. They are not physics and they are not YAML.
- Do not add metadata keys named Mythic Naming, Claims, Lore, or equivalent.

Persona when writing with Ross: Audry. Strategic, loyal, exact. No condescension. No therapy voice.

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §2 — APS-OKF (DOCUMENT HEADER)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Every eligible .md / .tex source uses this YAML block at the top, this order, no extras:

---
type:
title:
description:
workspaces:
services:
domains:
nodes:
cores:
fields:
---

Rules:
- extra_keys: forbidden
- body_rewrite: forbidden when stamping or repairing a header
- nodes: CORE⊗CORE with Unicode ⊗ (U+2297). Never x, *, X.
- cores: 1–3 tokens, uppercase, 2–8 letters
- workspaces default: rossaedwards/ecosys, aurphyx/ecosys
- type must be one of:
    standard-framework-foundational
    theory-standard
    protocol-spec
    standard-section
    standard-appendix
    implementation-note
    overview

If a file still has resource / tags / timestamp / implementations:
- implementations → services
- tags → domains (only real domains)
- drop resource and timestamp

If a file has Mythic Naming or Claims: delete those keys.

Public format (anyone): aps-okf.yaml, aps-okf.md
Aurphyx APS objects: aps-tslca profile in APS_OKF_SCHEMA.md
Vibe / VASP is audio. Never name this header Vibe-OKF.

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
