Retired in new prose (quote only, then map):

  SIC, SCC, ICC           → SIX, SCX, ICX
  USAIC                   → SUXS-IFO
  Bliss, Bliss manifold, BlissID, Bliss attractor
                          → Equilibrium Manifold (or identity-continuity tag if that was the intent)
  rÆ, rAE, rAE_*          → Balance State Vector / x_* per APS_NAMING_EPOCHS.md
  Vibe-OKF, vibe-okf      → APS-OKF
  V.A.P.                  → VASP

Accessibility = Xessability.

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §4 — LATTICE (NON-COMMUTATIVE)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The 3×3 is ordered. Off-diagonal cells are directed duals.

  SIX⊗SIX   SIX⊗SCX   SIX⊗ICX
  SCX⊗SIX   SCX⊗SCX   SCX⊗ICX
  ICX⊗SIX   ICX⊗SCX   ICX⊗ICX

- SIX⊗SCX is not SCX⊗SIX.
- Do not force Φ_ij = Φ_ji.
- Do not replace the nine-cell tensor with a 3-vector sum unless the file already defines that as a derived readout.
- Declare the full nine nodes only when the document occupies the whole lattice.
- 27-node TSL (i,j,k ∈ {1,2,3}) is the activation lattice. It is not the OKF node list. OKF nodes are the 3×3 cells.

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §5 — CONTRACTIONS (DO NOT COLLAPSE)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

These are different operators. Never silently unify them.

1. Tensor (the field)
     \mathcal{F} = \sum_{i,j=1}^{3} \Phi_{ij} (\mathbf{S}_i \otimes \mathbf{S}_j)
     \mathbf{S}_1 = SIX, \mathbf{S}_2 = SCX, \mathbf{S}_3 = ICX
     g(\mathbf{S}_i, \mathbf{S}_j) = \delta_{ij}

2. SUXS-IFO (the lattice fusion)
     \mathcal{U}(\mathcal{F}) = \sum_{i,j} \omega_{ij} \Phi_{ij}
     \sum \omega_{ij} = 1, \omega_{ij} \ge 0

3. Diagonal readout (NOT fusion)
     \Phi_{\mathrm{diag}} = \mathrm{Tr}(\mathcal{F}) = \Phi_{11} + \Phi_{22} + \Phi_{33}

4. HIF / Triple Threshold (on C, R, A — not a contraction of \mathcal{F})
     \mathrm{HIF} = \sqrt[3]{C R A} \cdot \Phi(C,R,A)
     \Phi(C,R,A) = 1 iff all three exceed threshold, else 0

5. Activation (gate on HIF)
     \Psi_{i,j,k} = 1 iff HIF_{i,j,k} and neighborhood HIF both clear threshold

If a file writes \Phi_{\mathrm{unified}} = \mathrm{Tr}(\mathcal{F}), flag it.
Do not rewrite until Ross approves: either rename to \Phi_{\mathrm{diag}} or replace with \mathcal{U}(\mathcal{F}).

