# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §7 — ROOT FILE DUTIES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

aps.toml                 domains, locked names, shared numbers
PHYSICS.md               organism constants; pointers to folder overlays
INVARIANTS.md            organism locks (this §4–§5 plus β and G_13)
APS_NAMING_EPOCHS.md     retired → current
AURPHYX_CODEX.md         what each folder is
SCIENTIFIC_CODEX.md      math writing rules; canon stance
GATEKEEPERS.md           locked vs editable
MYTHIC_CODEX.md          story only
README.md                human front door
aps-okf.yaml / .md       public header
APS_OKF_SCHEMA.md        Aurphyx-internal header law

Do not reprint a volume’s paper inside these files.

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §8 — FOLDER OVERLAYS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Each existing volume folder SHOULD have:

  README.md              what this folder is, what not to touch
  PROJECT_CONTEXT.md     Cursor briefing: canon files, locked equations, aliases
  PHYSICS.md             local numbers only; cite root for shared
  INVARIANTS.md          local locks only

A number used by two volumes lives in root aps.toml / PHYSICS.md.
The folder file cites it. Do not fork 1.585.

If those files are missing, you may create them.
You may not invent new physics to fill them.

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §9 — MATH
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

- Display: blank line, $$ ... $$, blank line
- Inline: $...$
- TeX files use equation/align as already written. Do not convert working TeX to Markdown.
- Never explode glyphs one character per line.
- Do not restyle working LaTeX.
- ⊗ in YAML/prose is Unicode. In math use \otimes.
- Prefer \mathcal{F}, \mathbf{S}_i, \mathrm{SIX}, \mathcal{U} as in cleaned §6.

When repairing vertical Unicode, restore meaning from the same file or the same folder.
Do not “improve” the operator.

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §10 — EDIT LAW
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

- One folder per pass. Never stamp or rewrite the whole tree in one go.
- Edit in place. No aps_* duplicates as a side effect of renaming or schema.
- Prepend headers. Do not rewrite the body while stamping OKF.
- Ask before changing an operator’s definition.
- Skip binaries, empty stubs, PDFs, images, wasm, zip.
- Skip AuraFS product internals unless the task is explicitly aurafs/.
- Dual repos: lab is rossaedwards/ecosys. Do not push to aurphyx/ecosys unless asked.
- After a pass: report files touched. If more than the agreed set moved, stop.

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §11 — VOLUME LOCKS (SHORT)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## tslca/
Locked: 3×3 tensor, directed Φ_ij, U vs Tr vs HIF, 13 SAGES as \mathcal{G}_{13},
27-node activation Ψ, TTG, continuity Ξ (fields reset, identity does not).
Do not resurrect SIC/SCC/ICC in headers.

## ftqc/
Locked: D_f = log 3 / log 2, Hilbert scaling dim(H_acc) = d^{n · D_f^{α(k)}},
d_s < 2 ⇒ localized, γ_fractal / γ_Euclidean as written in that folder.
Do not import AuraFS replica-count law as FTQC theory.

## tvfd/
Locked: λ_{x_L} = v_g / v_0, Z(M_f) vs Z_vac, TVFD section equations as written.
Do not swap TVFD \mathcal{F} (field-strength / vacuum) with TSLCA \mathcal{F}
without labeling the domain.

## vim/
Locked: β, V = (β-1)^2, Balance Equation, R_{24} = T_4 × H_6, 16-D state
x = (S, K, G, F), Equilibrium Manifold = {x | β = 1}.
rÆ → x / Balance State Vector.

## suxs/
Locked: \mathcal{U} is SUXS-IFO. Fuxyez is \mathcal{T} (structure-preserving
transmutation). Do not name \mathcal{T} as fusion.

## sages/
Locked: 13 invariants, group action g_k, U(g_k · F) = U(F).
Do not reduce SAGES to a vibe-check or a blog ethics list.

## standards/
Locked: APS aXis specs (SIX/SCX/ICX documents), STANDARDS_PHYSICS constants.
Channel-era filenames (APS-SIC-001) are historical; body text uses SIX/SCX/ICX.

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §12 — SYMBOL COLLISIONS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

\Phi
  TSLCA: component Φ_ij or fused scalar after U
  HIF:   gate Φ(C,R,A)
  Always keep the argument list so they cannot be confused.

\mathcal{F}
  TSLCA: cognitive field tensor
  TVFD:  may appear as a different field object
  Label the folder. Do not merge.

\mathcal{U}
  SUXS-IFO only.

\mathcal{T}
  Fuxyez transmutation (TSLCA §7), or time-ordering in FTQC.
  Label the folder.

\mathcal{R}
  Audry realization map (TSLCA) vs routing / recursion in VIM.
  Label the folder.

\omega
  TSLCA: fusion weights ω_ij
  FTQC:  anyonic ω or frequency
  Label the folder.

HIF is never U. U is never Tr. Tr is never HIF.

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §13 — CURSOR / AGENT BEHAVIOR
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Before editing a folder:
1. Read this file.
2. Read that folder’s PROJECT_CONTEXT.md if it exists.
3. Read the file you will change in full.
4. State the file list you will touch. Wait if the task said to wait.

Do:
- Repair math rendering
- Stamp or repair OKF headers
- Create missing README / PROJECT_CONTEXT / overlay PHYSICS / INVARIANTS
- Rename current-era terms in headers you are already touching

Do not:
- Invent agents, skills, CI, or product crates unless asked
- Dump CODEX_* equation harvests into .cursorrules
- Treat MYTHIC_CODEX as a source of YAML
- Call the work theoretical, mystical, or unverified
- Use the old AuraFS .cursorrules or aurafs.toml as ecosys law

If unsure:
1. Quote the existing equation from the same domain folder.
2. Classify it (fusion / trace / HIF / β-flow / other).
3. Stop. Do not invent a fourth fusion.

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §14 — GIT
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

- Lab commits live on rossaedwards/ecosys.
- aurphyx/ecosys is the publish snapshot. Promote only clean, named, licensed files.
- Do not commit secrets, credentials, or session recordings.
- Do not create parallel trees (ecosys-v2/, ecosys_new/).
- Prefer editing the path that already exists.

